	(text "Note to pump power connection:\n\nWhen using pump also check carefully AC-7b of your high power relay.\nThat value should be ideally slightly bigger than your pump wattage.\nFor example EZCT-20-20-230 has AC-7b at 7A, so it can be used to pumps with power of 1.2 kW\n\nObviously you have to ground your pump if it has metal parts exposed.\n\nIt is good practice to also add water flow sensor, so it can prevent pump from damaging itself when valve for any reason doesn't open and pump is working.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 91.186 45.466 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "1d112110-91ac-4175-bc0b-4c3b6f13e0be")
	)
	(text "Note:\n\nDepending on your relay board, you might connect JD-VCC to 5V instead 3.3V.\nOptoisolation should be considered to prevent damage of RPi.\nRead manual of your components.\n\n\nWhen selecting transformer to match your valves voltage, check inrush current draw.\nPGV-100-GB has inrush 0.37A, and hold 0.21A.\nTRM-24 has 0.62A max current output.\n\nPower coming from 230V Ac source on this schematic is already protected in home electrical instalation.\nIf you don't have any protections in your circuit, you should install them.\n\n\nIt is recommended to power RPi with good grade power adapter as bad one can cause micro shut downs.\n\nTo look at example connection made in real life, go to pictures folder.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.038 143.256 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ab67f837-b88d-4c2b-9723-9b180a98ef80")
	)
